hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1131","Chapter on dividing conquered land, 1171 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Were it not for the last of the Muslims, I would not have taken any town without dividing it, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided Khaybar."
